source: hh/tests/cli_conformance.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout)"
---
Faithfully play back a recorded session in an interactive TUI

Usage: hh replay [OPTIONS] [SESSION]

Arguments:
  [SESSION]  Session short id, full id, or `last` (most recent). Defaults to `last`

Options:
      --web        Export a self-contained HTML replay page and print its path, instead of opening the interactive TUI. Written to `<data_dir>/exports/hh-session-<id>.html` unless `-o` says otherwise. Does not need a terminal and does not start a server
  -o, --out <OUT>  With `--web`: write the page here instead (`-o -` writes the HTML to stdout)
      --open       With `--web`: open the page in your default browser. Only honoured when stdout is a terminal and `CI` is unset; never fails the command
      --no-open    Do not open a browser (the default; overrides an earlier `--open`)
  -h, --help       Print help

Examples:
  hh replay last               replay the most recent session
  hh replay a1b2c3             replay a session by short id
  hh replay last --web         write a self-contained HTML replay instead
  hh replay last --web --open  …and open it in your browser
